---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import ContentImage from '../components/ContentImage.astro'
import { NOW } from '../lib/site'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Tarlow is a solo developer in Portland, Oregon, building local-first tools and documenting the long way back."
  view="about"
>
  <main id="main-content">
    <article class="about">
      <header class="about-head">
        <div>
          <p class="label"><span class="label-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>About / the long way back</p>
          <h1>The long way <em>back.</em></h1>
          <p class="about-deck">
            On building, stepping away, and coming back to work in a purer way. A solo developer's notes
            from Portland, Oregon.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="about-portrait about-polaroid">
          <div class="portrait-orbit" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="portrait-frame">
            <ContentImage
              src="/images/grandma.png"
              alt="Tarlow as a young child with his grandmother, in an old Polaroid photograph"
              sizes="(max-width: 720px) 230px, 320px"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="portrait-cap">
            <span>Tarlow<br />Portland, OR</span>
            <span>Still becoming<br />under the same sky</span>
          </div>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="about-story">
        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-build">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">01</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The build</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-build">Building came first.</h2>
            <p>
              I've been building things since I was a kid - modding consoles, then computers, then
              websites - and I haven't really stopped since. My career started in internet marketing and
              web development, where I fell in love with automation: taking a repetitive, annoying task and
              making it disappear.
            </p>
            <p>
              In 2014 that turned into BoosterBots, a software company where I built Windows automation
              tools and custom systems for businesses. I spent years designing, shipping, and supporting
              desktop software for paying customers. It taught me more about building real products than
              anything I've done since.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-break">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">02</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The break</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-break">I stepped back.</h2>
            <p>
              The tools worked - that wasn't the problem. The problem was I was building software that
              fought the platforms it ran on, and I didn't want to spend my life doing that. I wanted to
              make things that are legitimately useful and won't get shut down.
            </p>
            <p>
              It was a revealing time, a vulnerable one, and honestly a scary one at times. But I found
              more of myself in that time, enough to grow into who I am today.
            </p>
            <p class="chapter-quote">"I took a break from everything, not a vacation."</p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-return">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">03</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The return</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-return">I came back wanting to help.</h2>
            <p>
              Somewhere in 2023 and 2024, AI tools got good enough to build real products with. I'd been
              watching the space for years, waiting for the technology to catch up to the ideas in my head.
              Suddenly it had.
            </p>
            <p>
              I shipped Handmade Checker, the first retail thing I'd built since I started developing
              again. I remembered how much I love building. I came back wanting to help other people grow
              too, and to work in a purer way.
            </p>
            <p>
              What I came back with is Moss AI Studio - my one-man shop for local-first,
              privacy-respecting tools. Same builder, same love of automation, but now I build things I can
              stand behind. I wrote the full story over at
              <a href="https://mossaistudio.com/blog/the-story-behind-moss-ai-studio/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moss AI Studio</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="chapter" aria-labelledby="chapter-work">
          <div class="chapter-side">
            <span class="chapter-num">04</span>
            <span class="chapter-name">The work</span>
          </div>
          <div class="chapter-copy">
            <h2 id="chapter-work">Moss grows slow.</h2>
            <p>
              Today the work is local-first tools for people who want their data to stay theirs:
              CopySprout, Handmade Checker, IndieGameScout, Moss Toolbox, Marimo Bot. When I'm not working
              on my own products, I take on custom builds and automation projects through the studio -
              turning clunky processes into clean, working systems for people who would rather not fight
              their own software.
            </p>
            <p>
              The name comes from moss. It grows slow, doesn't need much, and covers ground steadily. That
              is the kind of business I want to build - and the kind of life I'm trying to make room for.
              When I'm not at a keyboard, I'm usually in the Pacific Northwest: camping, fishing, or running
              with my dog Sunshine on the beach.
            </p>
          </div>
        </section>
      </div>

      <section class="about-quote-band" aria-label="A line from the story">
        <blockquote>
          "Coming back from a long break in tech was hard, but I'm growing, ready to help other people
          grow too, and to work in a <em>purer way.</em>"
        </blockquote>
        <p class="quote-attrib">From the about page / on the years away</p>
      </section>

      <section class="practice" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
        <div class="practice-head">
          <div>
            <p class="label"><span class="label-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>A small practice</p>
            <h2 id="practice-title">What I'm paying attention to.</h2>
          </div>
          <p>Not a productivity system. Just the three things that keep the work honest.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="practice-grid">
          <div class="practice-item">
            <span class="practice-index">01 / Attention</span>
            <h3>Be here for it.</h3>
            <p>The work gets better when I am actually here for it. Most of the craft is noticing.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-item">
            <span class="practice-index">02 / Patience</span>
            <h3>Grow slow.</h3>
            <p>Moss doesn't need much. It covers ground steadily. I keep coming back to that.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="practice-item">
            <span class="practice-index">03 / Outside</span>
            <h3>Leave the screen.</h3>
            <p>Trails, water, and a dog named Sunshine. The best ideas arrive away from the desk.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="about-now" aria-labelledby="about-now-title">
        <div>
          <p class="label"><span class="label-line" aria-hidden="true"></span>Now / {NOW.label}</p>
          <h2 id="about-now-title">Where I am <em>today.</em></h2>
          <p class="now-sub">
            Same builder. Same love of automation. A different set of questions about what the work is for.
          </p>
        </div>
        <ul class="now-list">
          <li><span class="now-key">Building</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.building}</span></li>
          <li><span class="now-key">Practicing</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.practicing}</span></li>
          <li><span class="now-key">At home</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.home}</span></li>
          <li><span class="now-key">Open to</span><span class="now-value">{NOW.openTo}</span></li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="about-contact" aria-labelledby="contact-title">
        <h2 id="contact-title">If this found you at the right time, say hello.</h2>
        <div class="contact-links">
          <a href="mailto:tarlow@mossaistudio.com">Email</a>
          <a href="https://mossaistudio.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Moss AI Studio ↗</a>
          <a href="https://github.com/DevTarlow/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub ↗</a>
          <a href="https://bsky.app/profile/mossaistudio.bsky.social" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Bluesky ↗</a>
          <a href="/rss.xml">RSS</a>
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
